{
  "_source": "UEV-A1 (docs/eras/uev.md, 'A1. Isotopes', machine 1, lines 1, 2, 29 and 30): the calutron's recipes and the GTM chemical reactor, mixer and assembler rows round them. Real processes: the Y-12 calutrons (electromagnetic separation of the ionised chloride, the isotopes caught in collector pockets); calcium-48 from the Lesnoy calutrons and ORNL's 2018 restart; HFIR-bred plutonium-244 (the target's plutonium-242 captures two neutrons) recovered by nitrate chemistry (Pu nitrate, oxide, chloride); electrodeposited actinide targets on aluminium foil.",
  "_how_it_is_used": [
    "Read by server_scripts/grindless/uev/isotopes.js at every server load. Each entry of types.<type>.recipes becomes one gtceu:<type> recipe, id grindless:<type>/<name>. calutron_separation rows carry the data key of the type = <name> (their EMI line). The programmed circuit picks the recipe: one per recipe inside calutron_separation (1-6); the GTM types use circuits 20 and up so GTM's own recipes cannot hide a row.",
    "itemsIn / itemsOut: { id, count }; fluidsIn / fluidsOut: { id, amount } in mB; kept: items never used up; charge: fluids never used up. eut x duration.",
    "Only from the calutron: gtceu:calcium_48_dust, gtceu:potassium_40_dust, gtceu:lithium_6_dust, gtceu:plutonium_244_dust (the collector pockets give the metal). The calutron's tails return to stock: Ca-40, K-39 and Li-7 come back as the natural chloride (GTM's calcium chloride, rock salt, lithium chloride, which the feeds start from); the depleted plutonium goes to IV's fuel fabrication plant through the MOX blend (tables/isotopes_fabrication.json, circuit 8).",
    "Line 2 loop: hot cell plutonium -> oxide -> calutron c6 (plutonium-242) -> target -> HFIR c4 (tables/isotopes_facility.json) -> facility c7 (nitrate) -> ZPM partitioning c3 (plutonium-244-rich oxide; the nitric acid comes back) -> chloride -> calutron c5 -> plutonium-244 -> oxide -> electrodeposited target. The fission products of the facility go to its evaporator (waste, ZPM's synroc).",
    "Destinations: the Ca-48 oven charge and the plutonium-244 target go to UEV's superheavy facility (A2); lithium-6 and potassium-40 go to the quantum gas lab; chlorine of the reductions and the HCl of the chlorinations go to GTM's chlorine and hydrochloric acid uses; the carbon dioxide and water of the calcite step go anywhere."
  ],
